{
  "manifest": "efe-mcp-manifest/0",
  "suite": "robocasa365",
  "kind": "rcb",
  "robot": "Franka Panda on an Omron mobile base with a torso lift (RoboCasa PandaOmron); the arm takes absolute joint position targets",
  "frame": {
    "suite": "the RoboCasa kitchen's world frame (metres, z up)",
    "quat": "wxyz",
    "base": {
      "fixed": [2.54253, -0.86372, 0.0, 0.000151, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0]
    },
    "base_text": "the mobile base's starting placement: on the floor at the base's origin, +X the way the arm faces, +Y the robot's left, +Z up; it stays where the base started (driving the base does not move this frame)"
  },
  "cameras": ["robot0_agentview_center", "robot0_agentview_left", "robot0_agentview_right", "robot0_eye_in_hand"],
  "default_cameras": ["robot0_agentview_center", "robot0_eye_in_hand"],
  "action_cameras": ["robot0_agentview_center"],
  "state_cameras": ["robot0_agentview_center"],
  "control": {
    "dt": 0.05,
    "control_dt": 0.05,
    "joint_speed": 0.6,
    "min_move_s": 0.5,
    "gripper_settle_s": 0.8,
    "settle_s": 0.2,
    "tolerance": {
      "joint": 0.03
    }
  },
  "types": {
    "joint_position": {
      "dim": 13,
      "hold": ["ref"],
      "hold_ref": {
        "names": ["cmd_arm_joint1", "cmd_arm_joint2", "cmd_arm_joint3", "cmd_arm_joint4", "cmd_arm_joint5", "cmd_arm_joint6", "cmd_arm_joint7", "cmd_grip", "cmd_base_x", "cmd_base_y", "cmd_base_yaw", "cmd_torso", "cmd_hybrid_mode"]
      },
      "zero_cols": [8, 9, 10, 11]
    }
  },
  "parts": {
    "arm": {
      "kind": "arm",
      "note": "Panda arm: 7 absolute joint position targets (rad); the gripper is open or closed only. There is no end-effector command.",
      "joints": {
        "type": "joint_position",
        "cols": [0, 7]
      },
      "gripper": {
        "type": "joint_position",
        "col": 7,
        "open": -1.0,
        "closed": 1.0,
        "binary": true
      },
      "state": {
        "joints": {
          "names": ["robot0_joint1_pos", "robot0_joint2_pos", "robot0_joint3_pos", "robot0_joint4_pos", "robot0_joint5_pos", "robot0_joint6_pos", "robot0_joint7_pos"]
        },
        "gripper": {
          "names": ["cmd_grip"],
          "open": -1.0,
          "closed": 1.0
        },
        "ee_pose": {
          "names": ["eef_right_x", "eef_right_y", "eef_right_z"]
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "notes": "The arm takes absolute joint position targets only (no end-effector command): describe_robot gives the joint limits. The base and the torso lift are driven with execute_trajectory space native, action_type joint_position (13 numbers, one row per 0.05 s control step): arm_joint1..7 (keep the current targets, cmd_* in proprio_now), grip (+1 closes, -1 opens), base_x, base_y, base_yaw (the mobile base's velocities in its own frame, normalised to [-1, 1]), torso (the lift's velocity, normalised), hybrid_mode (-1, the default). proprio_now has eef_right_x/y/z (the grip site's position in the world frame), the joints (robot0_joint1..7, mobilebase0_joint_mobile_forward/side/yaw, mobilebase0_joint_torso_height) and cmd_* (the last command). The poses the tools report are in the base's starting placement. The cameras ride on the robot; each frame comes with its current calibration.",
